cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the calibration framework it implements,
  please cite both the software and the manuscript below.
title: >-
  sparsegs / sparseGenSetCal: calibration for sparse gene-set scores
authors:
  - family-names: Tang
    given-names: Ming
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Radiation Oncology, Shenzhen Bao'an People's Hospital,
      The Second Affiliated Hospital of Shenzhen University, Shenzhen, China
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Xin
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Radiation Oncology, Shenzhen Bao'an People's Hospital,
      The Second Affiliated Hospital of Shenzhen University, Shenzhen, China
  - family-names: Duan
    given-names: Qiwen
    email: duanqiwen603@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-2231-6718"
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Radiation Oncology, Shenzhen Bao'an People's Hospital,
      The Second Affiliated Hospital of Shenzhen University, Shenzhen, China
    corresponding-indicator: true
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: >-
  https://example.invalid/sparse-gene-set-calibration
abstract: >-
  Python and R packages implementing a four-step calibration framework for
  sparse gene-set scores: the closed form for the tie-break level, three
  nested null families, the pre-flight check on the depth channel, and the
  decision table that selects a null method or refuses the analysis.
keywords:
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - gene-set scoring
  - AUCell
  - tie-breaking
  - null calibration
  - sparsity
